course: dictionary
lesson: 7880
title: Proper nouns and special names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name one particular person, place or time. These are proper nouns, and they start with a capital letter. «Ramadan» is one of these, because it is the name of one special month, so it begins with a big R. Words like month or fast are ordinary words and do not need a capital.
explain: The sentences around a word give you clues. «Ramadan, when many Muslims fast from dawn to sunset, starts about 11 days earlier each year on our calendar.» The words around it tell you that Ramadan is a time of year, and that many people fast during it.
explain: Context also helps with the meaning. Ramadan is the ninth month of the Islamic calendar, but it is also a time of prayer, giving to others and thinking about one's faith. «A friend fasting in Ramadan deserves kindness, never teasing.» The clue is that fasting is something a person does with care and respect.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or time, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Ramadan» means the ninth month of the Islamic calendar, when many Muslims fast.
fact: While fasting, Muslims do not eat or drink from dawn until sunset.
fact: The meal eaten after sunset during Ramadan is called iftar.
fact: The Islamic calendar follows the moon, so Ramadan moves about 11 days earlier each year and can fall in any season.
exercise: «Ramadan, when many Muslims fast from dawn to sunset, starts about 11 days earlier each year on our calendar.» What kind of word is Ramadan here? | A verb, a word for an action | An adjective, a word for describing | A question word | *A proper noun, the name of a special month
exercise: During Ramadan, when do many Muslims not eat or drink? | All night long | *From dawn until sunset | Only at lunchtime | Only on Sundays
exercise: Why does Ramadan start with a capital letter? | It is the longest word in the sentence | *It is the name of one special month | It is always the first word of a sentence | It is a colour
test: «Example: during Ramadan a girl in Birmingham fasts from dawn to sunset.» Which word is a proper noun? | during | fasts | girl | *Birmingham
test: What is the meal eaten after sunset during Ramadan called? | zakat | *iftar | breakfast | Eid
exam: Which sentence uses capital letters correctly? | sara fasted in ramadan this year. | *Sara fasted in Ramadan this year. | Sara fasted in ramadan this year. | sara fasted in Ramadan this year.
